# V03 midtone and wisp revision

Created with built-in image_gen, two edits of Polar_Distant_v02. Cloud_Polar_Midtones_Source.png preserves the generated straight RGBA. T_PaintedCloud_Midtones_v03.png is numerical channel packing for Unreal: R grayscale shade without the former /0.72 gain, G previous dissolution field bounded by new coverage, B previous module phase, A generated fractional coverage. Generative geometry alignment is approximate; silhouettes and wisps differ from the earlier version.

Applied as a new texture asset under /Game/RXSkySystem/Cubeless/PaintedCloud/v03/Evolution. Prior texture remains intact, and affected assets were backed up under Saved/PaintedEvolutionV03/BeforeMidtones_*. Existing blend, time, fog, and contrast controls retained. Growth now fades with baseline coverage to avoid promoting faint alpha speckles and wisp tails into visible outlines. Shader compilation and direct dependency checks passed. No new PIE result or full-repository verification is claimed; previous unrelated Niagara failure remains unresolved.

## Initial prompt

Star occlusion revision: alpha-composite draw order was already correct (SkyDome -100, CloudDome 10). Low cloud coverage transmitted bright background stars. Celestial opacity is now max(coverage, smoothstep(0.001,0.08,coverage)); premultiplied RGB reconstructs skyBackdrop at that opacity while the painted highlight retains its original coverage. This keeps the sky-blended appearance and strengthens sun/moon/star occlusion. Very faint outermost tails retain a soft transition. Midnight screenshot inspected, original editor time restored, material compile passed. Evidence: Saved/PaintedEvolutionV03/StarsNight_Review.png.

Edit this exact polar sky cloud texture. Preserve every cloud group's location, radial orientation, scale and silhouette, open central zenith and empty outer corners. Produce a production grayscale painted cloud texture on genuinely TRANSPARENT background with soft variable alpha. Keep hand-painted stylized illustration brushwork. Repaint interior shading to have abundant luminous middle tones: broad 40-75% gray rolling planes, selective 85-95% highlights and small 15-30% shadow pockets; rich readable internal transitions, not flat white cutouts, not uniformly darker clouds, no black contour or ambient-occlusion outline. All cumulus bodies should retain substantial coverage even in shaded parts; shading and opacity must be independent. Thin wisp clouds (the long narrow streaks and isolated slender clouds inside the ring) should have smooth long tapered opacity gradients from a visible bright-mid-gray core into completely transparent tips, softly dissolving into sky when composited. Do not depict wisps as dark gray opaque shards. Maintain the exact composition and hand-painted character, no 3D appearance, no cotton beads, no extra micro-noise, no sky color baked in, no text, no frames, no checkerboard painted into RGB. Square high resolution.

## Wisp refinement prompt

Refine this generated polar cloud texture. The large cumulus cloud internal midtone painting is good; keep their location and rich midtone painting. CRITICAL CORRECTION: the five isolated narrow clouds in the inner ring and the thin elongated wisps around the outer ring look like solid gray leaves with bright hard rims. Replace ONLY those thin wisps with airy hand-painted cirrus brush strokes: feathered flowing strands, wide soft opacity ramp along length, one diffuse rounded origin and very long tapered translucent tails, NO dark center, NO white outline, NO leaf-shaped enclosed contour. Wisp RGB should be light middle gray to near-white, the fading must be encoded in ALPHA, genuinely transparent background. Most of each wisp should be only 10-40% opacity with tiny 60% cores, tips zero opacity. Cumulus groups remain opaque with broad rolling 40-75% gray midtones, sparse highlights, and localized shadow pockets. Preserve the polar layout, empty center, radial orientations, scale, cloud positions. Remove any stray isolated pixel speckles in the transparent background. Output one clean square RGBA transparent texture, no text, no checkerboard.
